## Scenarios

### native-build worker minimal runtime imports

#### terminates non-worker invocation with the internal-entrypoint guard

- Verify: terminates non-worker invocation with the internal-entrypoint guard
   - Expected: result.exit_code equals `1)  # oracle: 1 — guard exits nonzero without the worker env`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 6 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-GEN-APP-001
step("Verify: terminates non-worker invocation with the internal-entrypoint guard")
val result = run("/mnt/data/worktrees/simple-main/bin/simple",
                 ["run", "src/app/cli/native_build_worker.spl"])
expect(result.exit_code).to_equal(1)  # oracle: 1 — guard exits nonzero without the worker env
expect(result.stdout + result.stderr).to_contain("internal entrypoint")
```

</details>

#### answers from the worker closure without the general CLI facade

- Verify: answers from the worker closure without the general CLI facade
- Importing the worker module and calling its exported arg helper runs the minimal closure
- The helper returns the argv tail (a text array), proving the worker entry resolves standalone
   - Expected: args.len() >= 0 is true


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 6 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
# @req: REQ-GEN-APP-001
step("Verify: answers from the worker closure without the general CLI facade")
step("Importing the worker module and calling its exported arg helper runs the minimal closure")
val args = native_build_entry_args()
step("The helper returns the argv tail (a text array), proving the worker entry resolves standalone")
expect(args.len() >= 0).to_equal(true)
```

</details>

